=== Prompt ===
Who is Kratos from God of War?

=== Response ===
Kratos is the main protagonist in the God of War video game series. He is a Spartan warrior who serves the Olympian gods, particularly Ares, in the first three games of the series.

Kratos is born into a family of Spartan warriors and is driven by a desire for revenge against his family's killers, who were actually Ares' minions. Throughout the series, Kratos goes through a series of transformations, from being a loyal servant of the Olympian gods to a rebellious hero seeking to overthrow them.

In the first game, Kratos kills his family, thinking they were the ones who killed his wife and child. He later discovers that they were actually Ares' minions. Kratos then sets out to kill Ares, who is responsible for the death of his family.

In the subsequent games, Kratos faces various gods and goddesses from Greek mythology, including Zeus, Poseidon, Athena, and others. He also encounters other characters, such as his son Atreus, whom he adopts in the 2018 game God of War.

Kratos is known for his brutal fighting style, his iconic Blades of Chaos, and his complex and often conflicted personality. He is also driven by a deep sense of anger, guilt, and regret, which often leads him to make difficult choices and confront his own demons.

Throughout the series, Kratos undergoes significant character development, transforming from a mindless killer to a more nuanced and empathetic hero. He becomes a symbol of the struggle between humanity and the gods, and his journey is a powerful exploration of the human condition.

The God of War series has received widespread critical acclaim for its engaging storylines, memorable characters, and intense action sequences. Kratos has become an iconic figure in the world of gaming, and his character has been widely praised for his complexity and depth.

